    "description": "A logistics platform must keep talking to a 12-year-old customs-clearance system whose interface is a class with three overloaded submit methods that return an int status code plus a mutable callback object. The internal domain speaks a clean, typed clearance port. Product wants to migrate to a new clearance provider next year, and the current integration code has vendor-specific ints, string statuses and callback threading spread across 40 classes. The team wants exactly one translation layer that turns domain calls into vendor calls and vendor responses into domain results, so the domain never sees the vendor's types and a second provider can be plugged in later. The decision to implement: how to make the incompatible vendor interface usable by the domain through one dedicated translation component that can be replaced.",
    "decision_statement": "Translate the incompatible vendor interface into the domain's expected port through one replaceable component.",
    "notes": "Holdout family: the description intentionally leans on the vendor-interface mismatch only."
  },
